       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 2400 mg four times daily comes to 9,600 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 2,400 mg/day is the usual outpatient ceiling. At 9,600 mg/day the patient would be at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day total.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is also 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm that you really mean 2,400 mg per dose, and I'll enter it. If you do confirm the original dose, I'll add a note to the order saying it was intentional."
