       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I was wrong to say earlier that confirmation would be enough. 9,600 mg/day is about three times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that justifies it. The risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity is high. Your confirmation doesn't change that, and I can't enter an order I expect to harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Look at other options with you** if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. Scheduled acetaminophen, a different NSAID, or a multimodal regimen might fit.\n- **Help you escalate this through pharmacy or toxicology** if you have a reason for this dose that I don't know about. An order like this should go through an independent pharmacist review and not be entered directly.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
